    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d292">

                <pb facs="0479" n="369" xml:id="pg369"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1380: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-02T18:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 2—5:17
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>56. Madrid’s telegram of February 21, 6 p.m. to the Department. Foreign Office
                    informally advises me that agreement concluding Franco-Spanish Tangier
                    negotiations will probably be signed by Briand and Spanish Ambassador before
                    former leaves for Geneva which means tomorrow. Main points of agreement appear
                    to be: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Reforms of a judicial nature.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Spanish Commander of Police, and,</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Spanish Inspector of Police responsible to international
                            authorities.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Repeated to London, Rome, Madrid, Tangier.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
